     EXPLANATION OF OPTION
 
     Use this option to format a logical unit when restoring a RAID 0 
     logical unit or a RAID 1, 3, or 5 logical unit with multiple-
     drive failures.  Note that the array controller automatically 
     formats the logical unit after you modify a logical unit 
     parameter requiring a format.
 
     CAUTION:  When you format a logical unit, ALL data on the logical 
               unit is lost.  For this reason, back up the data 
               file-by-file before formatting the logical unit (if
               possible).
 
     NOTE:  A procedure to format the logical unit is included
            in the help screens following the explanation of
            this option.
 
 
 
 
 
 
                                (CONTINUED)
     PROCEDURE -- FORMATTING A LOGICAL UNIT
 
     1.   Make sure you have backed up all the data on the logical 
          unit by copying it file-by-file to the back-up media (if
          possible).
 
     2.   Press "f" to format the logical unit.
 
     3.   Press "c" to confirm that you want to continue with 
          the format, or press "q" to quit.
 
     4.   Press "q" to quit ace.
 
     5.   Add the logical unit as a device by partitioning and 
          slicing it, and creating a filesystem(s) on the slice(s)
          if you want filesystems on the logical unit.
 
     6.   Copy your data to your logical unit from the back-up media 
          file-by-file.
 
     7.   Mount the filesystem.
 
